  "term": "Elavil",
  "definition": "Elavil refers to amitriptyline hydrochloride, a tricyclic antidepressant. It acts in the central nervous system by limiting the reuptake of norepinephrine and serotonin, raising their signaling levels, and it may also have pain-relieving effects.",
